<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Privacy Policy" description="What HSL Lab (hslab.space) and its blog handle through comments, visit statistics and ads, why, how long it is kept, cookies and how to opt out.">
  <header class="page-top"><div class="article-shell"><div class="section-kicker">Policy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>HSL Lab and its blog have no accounts. The site itself handles only the minimum needed for comments and visit statistics; ads on articles and project pages are served by Google, which uses cookies.</p></div></header>
  <div class="article-body article-shell">
    <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Comments</strong>: nickname, comment text, time posted, password (stored only as an irreversible hash), and a hashed IP value for spam control (the IP address itself is not stored)</li>
      <li><strong>Visit statistics</strong>: the article address visited and daily view counts. No cookies, IP addresses or device identifiers are stored</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>2. Why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To publish comments and confirm the author when deleting (nickname and password must match)</li>
      <li>To prevent flooding and spam</li>
      <li>To understand which articles and pages are read and improve the site</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>3. How long</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Comments stay until the author or the operator deletes them. Deletion is immediate; a comment with replies remains only as "deleted"</li>
      <li>Hashed IP values are erased automatically 30 days after posting</li>
      <li>Visit statistics are kept only as aggregate counts that cannot identify anyone</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>4. Sharing and processors</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or share this information. The site and its database run on Cloudflare, Inc. infrastructure, so data may be processed and stored outside Korea, including in the United States.</p>
    <p>Map images on the weather forecast project page are loaded by your browser directly from the OpenStreetMap Foundation tile server (map data © OpenStreetMap contributors), which can receive your IP address and browser details.</p>
    <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
    <p>Articles, project pages and project stories may show Google AdSense ads (the portfolio and home page carry none). Google and its ad partners use cookies or similar technology to choose ads based on visits to this and other sites, to measure impressions and clicks, and to prevent fraud. Google collects and processes this information itself, not the operator; see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You can turn off personalized ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>, and opt out of other vendors' personalized ads at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a></li>
      <li>Visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland see Google's consent message first; without consent, no personalized-ad cookies are used</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>6. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>The operator sets no cookies of its own. Pages with ads may use the Google advertising cookies in section 5, which you can block or delete in your browser. Your theme setting and comment nickname are kept only in your browser's localStorage; they are not sent to the server and you can clear them at any time.</p>
    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can delete your comment at any time with the nickname and password you entered</li>
      <li>If you forgot the nickname or password, leave a comment on the same article asking for deletion and the operator will remove it</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>8. Responsible person</h2>
    <p>The operator, HSL, is responsible for personal information handling. Requests are handled through the method in section 7 or by email to <a href="mailto:coolwin200@gmail.com">coolwin200@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>9. Effective date</h2>
    <p>This policy applies from October 24, 2026 (Google AdSense ads added); the previous version applied from October 16, 2026. Changes will be announced on this page with a new effective date.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
